# MashLab AI Mashup Engine Rule

- Professional DJ-assistant mashup engine — not a one-button toy.
- Hybrid: music analysis + DSP + AI stem separation. No single magic end-to-end model.
- DJ-ready draft quality goal; manual override for beatgrid, BPM, key, phrases, stems, transitions, EQ/fades, render quality.

## Canonical state (already shipped)

- RC4: section picker
- RC6: Remix Brain / DJ sync
- RC7: Arrangement Brain (Clean Blend, Hook Remix, DJ Edit)
- Windows Desktop RC1 (`mashlab-windows-desktop-rc1` @ master `dd24daa`)
- Import, metadata, Demucs stems, FFmpeg/Rubber Band export, Quick Mix path exist

## Pipeline north star

import → analyze (BPM/key/structure) → anchor → stems → align → stretch/pitch → transition render → QC → export + metadata

## Guardrails

- **Do not rebuild** import/stem/Remix Brain/Arrangement Brain unless fixing a specific bug or scoped extension.
- **Branch from canonical `master`** — no parallel rewrite app or unrelated history.
- License notes (GPL/AGPL, Rubber Band, Essentia) apply to **packaging/distribution**, not local dev unless bundling into a ship artifact.
- Local-only, rights-neutral scope preserved.

## Next phase

**Phase 45 — Windows First-Run Setup Assistant:** guide desktop users through venv, Demucs/PyTorch, FFmpeg/ffprobe, Rubber Band, PATH, sidecar startup, port conflicts.

## Anti-goals

No generative AI music creation, end-to-end neural mashup models, social/cloud features, or perfect-automation claims.
